// Starting-point project config for OpenCode. The `init` skill copies this
// file to `opencode.jsonc` on first run if `opencode.jsonc` is missing. After
// that, edit `opencode.jsonc` (not this template). `opencode.jsonc` is
// gitignored, like the other harnesses' runtime files; this template stays
// committed so the repo documents itself.
//
// OpenCode reads `AGENTS.md` at the repo root on its own, so this file holds
// only what `AGENTS.md` cannot: MCP servers. The model, providers and
// permissions belong in your user-level OpenCode config, not here.
//
// Superagent needs no MCP server for the quick-start. Each source declares
// its own MCP or CLI requirements (superagent/docs/data-sources.md). Browser
// automation is not an MCP: it runs through the browserctl CLI.
//
// To enable a server, add it under `mcp.servers` and restart OpenCode.
// Example: the Gmail server the email skills use. The command resolves
// `gmail-mcp` from PATH after putting the machine-local Node install first,
// so one line works on every machine (see data-sources.md, "Gmail"):
//
//   "gmail": {
//     "type": "local",
//     "command": ["sh", "-c", "PATH=\"$HOME/.superagent/tools/node/bin:$PATH\" exec gmail-mcp"]
//   }
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "servers": {}
  }
}
